6) Questlines
6.1 Entry: The Troupe’s Escort

Rescue performers to gain pass.queen_intro. Fail path: Underground/miner scramble; distrust flags.

6.2 The Queen’s Illness (major)

A) Cure and Expose: trace taint → flip Jorren → get ledger (steal/bribe) → confront Velira at bathhouse.
Result: Stability +2, Matriarchy ++, Merchant −, rare-cure queue opens, palace fast lane; illness.resolution=cured.

B) Too Late / Fail: wrong lead/missed windows → regent (Selinne or merchant proxy).
Result: Stability −2, Merchant ++, Cult +, nobles +20% prices, curfews; illness.resolution=dead.

C) Complicity: assist merchants with fake “stabilizer”; remove loyal duchess via Assassin contract.
Result: Underground +, Merchant +, permanent −100 cap on Matriarchy ceiling; archive key; illness.resolution=regent.

6.3 Merchant War (major)

Weight of a City: bug scales → MPI +15, Stability +1.

Pay Dirt: broker miner co-op with Mira → co-op vendor, MPI +20, Merchant −.

The Long Buyout: help Hareth secure 3 warehouses → MPI −25, Merchant +, small Underground + via kickbacks.

6.4 Black Market & Guilds (major, optional)

Entry via rune + fee or Orlen vouch after “Seized Home.”

Contracts have a 48h counter-contract window from opposing factions.

Silent Skylight: remove palace archivist (30% later hit on you).

Red Ledger: steal Merchant assay ledger; deliver to Deyla (Underground +) or Matriarchy (Matriarchy +, Underground −).

Thieves Charter: “People’s Cut” redirects 30% heists to village relief; fewer citizen thefts, more merchant raids.

6.5 Cult of Orion (major, optional)

False Blessing: +2 initiative then “Speed Debt” skips one action for 3 encounters.

Exposé path: retrieve temple records → public debate mini-challenge.
Win: cultPressure −20, Stability +1, access to genuine temple lore.
Lose: 24h harassment; palace DCs +2; retry after acquiring missing proof.

6.6 Street Stories (modular by Stability)

≤ −2: Bread Riot, Clinic Queue Stampede, Eviction Night.

−1..+1: Sick Child, Seized Home, Urchin Band.

≥ +2: Community Feast, Volunteer Patrols, Surgeons need reagents.

