10) Grid & Generation
10.1 Grid model

Size: default 16×16 cells.

Cell schema: id, x,y, terrainTag, elevation, cover, sandShiftable, travelCost, visibility, hazardWeight, encounterTier, poiId, spawnTableId

Terrain tags: dune_sea, rocky_ridge, obsidian_field, oasis_basin, ruin_cluster, salt_flat, caravan_track

Movement costs: dune +0.5, ridge +0.25, obsidian +0.75, salt −0.25, caravan −0.5 (base 1)

Visibility: base 3 cells; storms reduce to 1.

10.2 Navigation & Sandshift

rollForecast() reveals storm corridor 2–4 cells ahead; highlights low-cost routes.

track.sandShift: storms +40; every +25 triggers swaps for sandShiftable corridors; oases/temples/gauntlet fixed.

10.3 Fast travel

Unlock at Oases, Watchtowers, Gauntlet forecourt; night use requires Stability ≥ −1.

10.4 Generation pipeline (seedable)

Seed: e.g., ALACAI-SEED-7F.

Inner 8×8: dunes/ridges 60/40.

East wedge: obsidian_field near wyvern caverns.

Oasis pockets south/northwest (2–3 cells each).

Two salt_flat lanes as fast corridors.

City gate on west edge; Outskirts one cell east.

Caravan tracks 2–3 winding routes gate→oases→Weight spur.

Gauntlet forecourt: 6–10 cells from gate, ridge/ruin boundary, ≥4 cells from any temple.

Five temples: min 5-cell separation; one near obsidian, one dunes, one oasis rim, one embedded ruin, one salt edge.

Spawn minor POIs: watchtowers, bandit camps, scavenger pits, collapsed tunnels.

Assign spawnTableId by terrain/region; mark miniboss patrol graph along open terrain and salt flats.

Bake travelCost/cover/hazardWeight.

